Hi Devin,

If those numbers are correct, then this is what you would expect with effective sample sizes on the order of a thousand—not much difference between the KDEc and AKDEc point estimates. Only the lowest performance home-range estimators still have substantial bias with that quality of data. With the buffalo, the effective sample sizes are on the order of 20. Yes, there are also a thousand locations sampled, but it takes the buffalo a 1-2 weeks to cross its range.

Since this is a squirrel, you might want to check the impact of location error. It's probably okay, though, at this sampling rate.

Best,
Chris

