Hi Steve,

I find that RAM isn't an issue unless making very detailed distributions for plotting. To save computation time, I recommend making a for loop over individuals and then upgrading that to a foreach loop to parallelize over CPU cores.

Continuous-time methods are made exactly for challenges like having different temporal resolutions. So don't worry about it. Uncertainties will propagate through the confidence intervals.

For manual inspection, you might look at these functions: https://ctmm-initiative.github.io/ctmm/reference/select.html
For something more automated/objective, you might consider the segclust2d package.

Best,
Chris

